WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:07.182
Welcome to Computer Class. Today you will learn how to add a list of numbers in Excel using the SUM formula.

2
00:00:07.482 --> 00:00:13.559
Open Excel on your own computer and follow each step with me. It takes only five minutes.

3
00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:20.198
Why do we use a formula? Excel adds the numbers for you, quickly and without mistakes.

4
00:00:20.498 --> 00:00:27.132
If a price changes, the total updates by itself. Shops, schools and offices use this every day.

5
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:33.848
Step one. Type your data. Put the item names in column A and the prices in column B.

6
00:00:34.148 --> 00:00:39.877
Click a cell, type the word or number, and press Enter to go down. Type Total in cell A6.

7
00:00:40.883 --> 00:00:46.975
Step two. Click the cell where you want the answer. Here, click cell B six, next to the word Total.

8
00:00:47.275 --> 00:00:50.412
The green box shows which cell is selected.

9
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:58.855
Step three. Type an equals sign, then S U M, then an open bracket. Type B two, a colon, B five, and close the bracket.

10
00:00:59.155 --> 00:01:03.976
The formula means: add all the numbers from cell B two to cell B five.

11
00:01:04.276 --> 00:01:06.879
Always start a formula with the equals sign.

12
00:01:07.883 --> 00:01:15.150
Step four. Press Enter. Excel shows the answer, fourteen point five. That is the total of all four prices.

13
00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:24.720
Try it. Change the price of eggs to six. Watch the total. It changes to seventeen by itself. This is the power of a formula.

14
00:01:25.717 --> 00:01:32.746
Now it is your turn. Make a list of five things you buy each week, add the prices, and use SUM to find the total.

15
00:01:33.046 --> 00:01:39.010
For a challenge, try the AVERAGE formula. Remember to start with the equals sign. Great work!

